## Quickstart

Requirements: [git](https://git-scm.com), [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) and
[Task](https://taskfile.dev).

```bash
task setup          # environment, git hooks and agent plugins
task check          # lint, types, import contracts and tests
task run            # run the pipeline on data/01_raw/input.csv
```

`task --list` shows every task.

## Working with coding agents

The project is set up for Claude Code and Codex. `AGENTS.md` holds the rules for both.

1. Describe the change. The agent brainstorms and writes a plan to `docs/plans/`.
2. Durable decisions become ADRs in `docs/adr/`.
3. The `deliver` skill executes the approved plan until every item is done and `task check`
   passes.
4. `cross-review` has the other vendor's agent review the result once.

For unattended runs: commit the plan and run `task deliver`. It works in a separate worktree and
opens a GitHub pull request once the check and the review pass.

## Documentation

`task docs:serve` serves the documentation: context, evaluation protocol, decisions and the
API reference.

